    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as our clear focal point; his 84.02 score against Bibee is the highest on the board, bolstered by a prime leadoff spot and a significant platoon advantage that keeps him in \"Elite\" territory. Joining him at the top of our offensive engine, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **Brice Turang** (73.40) represent high-efficiency plays. **Mickey Moniak** benefits immensely from a favorable park factor (+14%) and platoon alignment against Wacha, while **Brice Turang**\u2019s elite sprint speed and leadoff placement override the negative impact of facing a catcher with a sub-2.0s pop time, ensuring we remain aggressive on the basepaths. **James Wood** also warrants attention with an \"Elite\" xwOBA of 0.423, providing a stable, high-floor presence at the top of the order against Bryce Elder.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Austin Riley**, whose 49.17 score left him just shy of the \"Strong\" start threshold. While his power upside is usually undeniable, the combination of a difficult matchup against Foster Griffin and an assumed lower-order batting position pushed the optimizer to prioritize the platoon-boosted efficiency of **Zach McKinstry** and **Jose Caballero**. We must monitor the lineup cards closely for **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Cole Young**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Mickey Moniak**, **James Wood**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Henry Bolte**; all are currently \"Lineup Pending,\" and any shifts that drop these players in the order\u2014particularly **Brice Turang** or **James Wood**\u2014will force a re-evaluation of our daily ceiling. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains sidelined on the IL, our current alignment maximizes our exposure to favorable SP_xERA matchups, specifically targeting the vulnerabilities of the starters facing **Zach McKinstry** and **Brice Turang**.",
